cost                 package:AA                      R Documentation

Cost Data

Description:

     The 'cost' data frame has 31 rows and 2 columns.

     It gives the costs of treatment for two groups of patients with a
     history of deliberate self harm.  One group received the usual
     therapy, and the other received cognitive behavioural therapy. 
     The data were collected to compare the costs of the two
     treatments.

Usage:

     data(cost)

Format:

     This data frame contains the following columns:

     'f' group number;

     'y' costs (pounds sterling) of cognitive behavioural therapy
          (group 1) and of the usual therapy (group 2) for patients
          with a history of  deliberate self harm.

Source:

     The data were obtained from

     Evans, K., Tyrer, P., Catalan, J. _et al._ (1999). 
     Manual-assisted-cognitive-behavaviour therapy in the treatment of
     recurrent deliberate self harm: A randomised controlled trial. 
     _Psychological Medicine_, *29*, 19-25.

References:

     Brazzale, A.R., Davison, A.C. and Reid, N. (2007).  _Applied 
     Asymptotics: Case Studies in Small-Sample Statistics_.  Cambridge 
     University Press, Cambridge.  Example 3.5.

Examples:

     data(cost)
     plot(y ~ factor(f), data = cost, xlab = "therapy", ylab = "cost of therapy")
